    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1769": {
      "title": "Chemistry Outreach Coordinator",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Chemistry Outreach Coordinator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Chemistry Outreach Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Why Join Us? At Juniata College, you'll be part of a passionate team bringing quality STEM education to communities that need it most. If you're looking to make a difference in the lives of students and teachers—and have a background in science education—this is the role for you! Apply today to be a key part of our mission-driven outreach team. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Chemistry Outreach Coordinator Posting Number 20110652 Pay Rate Starting at $23,160 (over 10 mos) Position Type Part Time/Temporary Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Join Juniata College’s nationally recognized Science In Motion ( SIM ) program as a Part-time Chemistry Outreach Coordinator and help bring hands-on, high-impact science education to local school districts. The Chemistry Outreach Coordinator plays a vital role in sustaining and expanding SIM’s chemistry-focused outreach efforts. This part-time position is essential to maintaining our existing partnerships and fulfilling contractual commitments to participating schools. Key Responsibilities: Provide Science In Motion ( SIM ) chemistry education services 3 days per week in accordance with Pennsylvania Department of Education ( PDE ) contracts Coordinate and implement outreach initiatives and lab programs for local schools Hire, train, and supervise Juniata College student employees Oversee the scheduling, delivery, and maintenance of outreach equipment Serve as a consultant to local teachers to support and enhance science education in the classroom The Chemistry Outreach Coordinator is a part time 10-month position with no benefits and annual renewal based upon performance and funding. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..…EOE Position Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Chemistry, Education, or a related scientific discipline Excellent organizational and time-management skills Strong interpersonal and written communication skills Ability to work independently and as part of a team Understanding of Juniata College’s mission and outreach vision Valid driver’s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Supervision Required/Given This role reports directly to the Outreach Director and works collaboratively with other STEM coordinators on campus. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working in educational outreach or similar programs Pennsylvania teaching certification Classroom teaching experience Physical Demands Ability to unload and reload vehicle, push/pull loaded carts, usually lift up to 20-lbs and sometimes up to 50-lbs. Special Instructions to Applicants Why Join Us? At Juniata College, you’ll be part of a passionate team bringing quality STEM education to communities that need it most. If you’re looking to make a difference in the lives of students and teachers—and have a background in science education—this is the role for you! Apply today to be a key part of our mission-driven outreach team. Posting Detail Information Open Date 02/05/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1840": {
      "title": "Assistant Field Hockey Coach",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Assistant Field Hockey Coach Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Field Hockey Coach Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. It is Juniata College’s policy to conduct background checks. Valid driver’s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Field Hockey Coach Posting Number 20110679 Pay Rate Monthly stipend plus room and board Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College, an NCAA Division III Institution, invites applications for a full-time Assistant Field Hockey Coach-Intern. This is a 12-month position that includes a monthly stipend, room, board and full benefits. Juniata is a co-educational, liberal arts college and highly regarded for its academic excellence. Responsibilities include but are not limited to; assisting the Head Field Hockey Coach with all operations of the field hockey program, including but not limited to, recruiting, athlete and team development, practice planning, academic monitoring, team travel and meet management. Key Responsibilities: Leading recruiting responsibilities: “Recruiting Coordinator” – communication with PSAs, database management, visit planning, and calendar scheduling. Coordinating travel arrangements: meals, lodging, practices. Supporting all practice and match preparations. Conducting individual workouts and team skill development sessions. Contributing to scouting, game-day strategy, and in-game decision making. Assisting with summer camps, fundraising, and alumni engagement. Participating in departmental functions and committee work as needed. Supporting athletic operations and game-day management. Other duties as assigned by the Athletic Director/Field Hockey Coach. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status… EOE Position Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree required One to Three years of collegiate coaching &/or playing experience preferred Knowledge and understanding of NCAA (and Landmark Conference) rules, regulations, and the Division III philosophy. Demonstrated ability to coach, recruit, manage, and contribute to a competitive college field hockey program. Valid driver’s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Supervision Required/Given This position reports to the Head Field Hockey Coach. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants It is Juniata College’s policy to conduct background checks. Valid driver’s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/08/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
