    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1834": {
      "title": "Head Women&#39;s Lacrosse Coach",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Head Women&#39;s Lacrosse Coach Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Head Women's Lacrosse Coach Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Juniata’s Full-Time Benefits package prioritizes the well-being and work-life balance of employees: Medical; vision; dental; retirement (403b); paid vacation, sick leave, holiday time; tuition benefit (employee, spouse and dependents); wellness programming; and additional insurance programs. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Head Women's Lacrosse Coach Posting Number 20110676 Pay Rate Starting at $53,400 Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College invites applications for the position of Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach. Juniata is a co-educational, liberal arts college, highly regarded for its academic excellence, with an enrollment of 1,300 students. Juniata is a founding member of the highly regarded Landmark Conference, which is committed to conducting intercollegiate athletics programs in a way that recognizes, as paramount, the centrality of the academic mission at each member institution. Primary Role: Responsible for the development and maintenance of the lacrosse program. This includes structural and administrative organization of the program as outlined below. Typical Duties and Responsibilities: · Provide vision and build a positive team culture committed to the welfare of our student-athletes, a positive representation of the college, academic excellence, citizenship, and competitive success. · Practice organization, planning, scheduling, preparation, and execution. · Develop and implement specific training and skill development programs. · Prepare the team for competitions including; scouting reports, meetings, and instruction. · Develop and implement appropriate in-competition coaching techniques and strategies. · Recruit and retain qualified student-athletes. · Develop and meet recruiting goals in consultation with the Director of Athletics. · Maintain roster sizes in accordance with agreed upon maximum and minimum roster ranges. · Provide support, oversight, assistance, to student-athletes with regards to academic performance, planning, and success. · Meet department standards for academic success. · Effectively manage all aspects of the program’s budget including the purchase of all athletic equipment and supplies, and the management of the programs travel and recruiting budgets. · Hire, train, mentor, assistant coaches, student-assistants, and student managers. · Schedule all non-traditional and traditional competitions and practices. · Develop, recommend, and enforce appropriate levels of discipline, behavior, rules, regulations, and conduct. · Serve as team spokesman and appropriately represent the program and the college on campus and in the community. · Ensure adherence to the rules, regulations, and policies of all governing bodies—Juniata College Athletics, Juniata College, Landmark Conference, and National Collegiate Athletic Association. · Participate in overall administration of the Athletics Department by representing the office as requested and cooperatively assisting colleagues. This includes attending all mandatory department activities and functions, membership on department and campus committees, and participation upon request in enrollment, fundraising, and/or promotional events. · Serve as game/event manager as requested. · Other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..…EOE Position Qualifications · Knowledge and capabilities normally acquired through completion of a Bachelor’s Degree or an equivalent combination of education and experience. · Knowledge and understanding of NCAA rules, regulations, and the Division III philosophy. · Three to five years of collegiate coaching &/or playing experience. · Demonstrated ability to teach, strategize, recruit, lead, manage, represent, and oversee a nationally competitive athletic program. - Valid driver’s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. - Must achieve satisfactory results from a background check Supervision Required/Given Receives direct supervision from the Director of Athletics. Works collaboratively and supportively with other individuals and groups. Hires, trains, and supervises assistant coaches, and student coaches, student managers, providing specific direction and oversight of assignments and responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Juniata’s Full-Time Benefits package prioritizes the well-being and work-life balance of employees: Medical; vision; dental; retirement (403b); paid vacation, sick leave, holiday time; tuition benefit (employee, spouse and dependents); wellness programming; and additional insurance programs. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/16/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1843": {
      "title": "Director of Public Safety",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Director of Public Safety Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director of Public Safety Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Why Juniata? At Juniata, public safety is about more than responding to incidents—it’s about building a campus environment where people feel safe, supported, and able to thrive. The Director will have an opportunity to shape campus safety practices, strengthen partnerships across the College, and contribute to the overall student experience. Comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, retirement (403b), paid vacation and holidays, tuition benefits for employees and dependents, wellness programs, and more. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director of Public Safety Posting Number 20110680 Pay Rate Salary commensurate with experience Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College is seeking a collaborative, experienced leader to serve as Director of Public Safety . This position provides strategic and operational leadership for campus safety and security, helping create a safe, welcoming environment where students, faculty, and staff can live, learn, and work. Reporting to the Vice President for Student Life and Dean of Students, the Director leads Public Safety personnel and operations while partnering across campus and with local law enforcement, emergency services, and community agencies. What You’ll Do Lead the daily operations, staffing, training, supervision, and professional development of Public Safety personnel supporting a 24/7 campus operation. Develop and implement strategies, policies, and procedures that promote campus safety, security, emergency preparedness, and crime prevention. Serve as the College’s Clery compliance officer, overseeing crime reporting, Campus Security Authority ( CSA ) training, and related federal and state requirements. Coordinate the College’s emergency communications and emergency operations efforts, serving as a key liaison with law enforcement, fire, EMS , and emergency dispatch agencies. Partner with Student Life and other campus leaders on student conduct, crisis response, investigations, and after-hours emergency situations. Plan security and emergency response for campus events and provide safety training and education to students, faculty, and staff. Build collaborative relationships with victim advocacy and support services and promote trauma-informed responses to incidents. Develop and manage the Public Safety budget and ensure effective stewardship of departmental resources. Oversee departmental communications, reporting, records, crime statistics, policies, and compliance documentation. Foster a culture of belonging, inclusion, respect, and well-being throughout campus. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..…EOE Position Qualifications What We’re Looking For Bachelor’s degree in criminal justice, social work, student affairs, or a related field; advanced study or equivalent professional experience preferred. 5–7+ years of progressively responsible experience in public safety, law enforcement, campus safety, student affairs, or a related field. Demonstrated experience supervising personnel and managing departmental budgets and operations. Knowledge of the Clery Act, Title IX, VAWA , Title VII , and applicable federal, state, and local safety requirements. Experience with emergency management, crisis response, investigations, and/or campus safety programming. Strong interpersonal, communication, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively with students, families, faculty, staff, administrators, and external partners. A collaborative, inclusive, and transparent leadership style with a demonstrated ability to build trust and foster positive change. Commitment to the residential liberal arts college experience and to creating a safe and supportive campus community. Valid driver’s license and successful completion of a background investigation. Supervision Required/Given Reports directly to the Vice President for Student Life and Dean of Students. Receives general direction and guidance while working with independent discretion. Direct supervision of full-time and part-time public safety officers and personnel. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Why Juniata? At Juniata, public safety is about more than responding to incidents—it’s about building a campus environment where people feel safe, supported, and able to thrive. The Director will have an opportunity to shape campus safety practices, strengthen partnerships across the College, and contribute to the overall student experience. Comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, retirement (403b), paid vacation and holidays, tuition benefits for employees and dependents, wellness programs, and more. Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/31/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1854": {
      "title": "Provost",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Provost Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Provost Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications, Nominations, and Inquiries Academic Search is partnering with Juniata College in this search . Confidential discussions about the position are welcome and may be arranged by contacting Senior Consultant Dr. Stuart Dorsey: Stuart.Dorsey@academicsearch.org Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . A search profile with detailed information about Juniata College, leadership agenda, and required and preferred qualifications for the next provost is available for download here . Nominations and inquiries may be sent to JuniataProvost@academicsearch.org . To apply, candidates should submit two separate documents (in PDF format): (1) a detailed cover letter, addressed to the Search Committee, expressing interest in this position and addressing how you meet the qualifications as outlined in the search profile, and (2) a current resume/curriculum vitae. The position will remain open until filled but only applications received by November 2, 2006. Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . Posting Details Position Information Job Title Provost Posting Number 20110684 Pay Rate Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Academic Search is partnering with Juniata College in this search . Confidential discussions about the position are welcome and may be arranged by contacting Senior Consultant Dr. Stuart Dorsey: Stuart.Dorsey@academicsearch.org Juniata College’s new provost will join an institution ranked among the nation’s top 100 liberal arts colleges and supported by a stable financial outlook and consistent leadership. Dr. James Troha is entering his 14th year as president, and the current provost, Dr. Lauren Bowen, is in her 13th year. Juniata’s faculty and staff are exceptionally student-centered, and its liberal arts academic model is distinctively interdisciplinary. The College seeks a new provost with strong and compelling academic credentials who will advance academic quality and inspire excellence in teaching and learning. The new provost must have exceptional budget management skills and be able to make decisions, communicate with openness, honesty, and transparency, engage stakeholders in meaningful dialogue, and manage change with empathy. As a member of the senior leadership team, the provost will serve as the chief advocate for faculty and academic programs and as a key partner to the president in institutional decision-making. The provost will be the clear leader, advocate, mentor, and public face of the faculty and academic program, maintaining a highly visible and accessible presence across the College. As Juniata’s chief academic officer, the provost reports to the president and provides visionary leadership for the academic enterprise, advancing academic excellence and innovation while strengthening the College’s longstanding tradition of individualized education. Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . A search profile with detailed information about Juniata College, leadership agenda, and required and preferred qualifications for the next provost is available for download here . Position Qualifications An earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution. A record of academic achievement, scholarship, and professional accomplishment sufficient to earn the respect and credibility of faculty colleagues. A minimum of five years of progressively responsible academic leadership experience in higher education, such as service as a department chair, division head, dean, associate dean, associate provost, or in a comparable leadership role. A search profile with detailed information about Juniata College, leadership agenda, and required and preferred qualifications for the next provost is available for download here . Supervision Required/Given Reflecting the breadth of the academic enterprise, direct reports to the provost include the associate provost, the assistant vice president of institutional effectiveness, the director of the learning commons, the museum director, the dean of international education, the director of Baker Institute, the laboratory coordinator, the director of community engaged learning, the registrar, the director of advising, the director of the Raystown Field Station, and the assistant to the provost. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Applications, Nominations, and Inquiries Academic Search is partnering with Juniata College in this search . Confidential discussions about the position are welcome and may be arranged by contacting Senior Consultant Dr. Stuart Dorsey: Stuart.Dorsey@academicsearch.org Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . A search profile with detailed information about Juniata College, leadership agenda, and required and preferred qualifications for the next provost is available for download here . Nominations and inquiries may be sent to JuniataProvost@academicsearch.org . To apply, candidates should submit two separate documents (in PDF format): (1) a detailed cover letter, addressed to the Search Committee, expressing interest in this position and addressing how you meet the qualifications as outlined in the search profile, and (2) a current resume/curriculum vitae. The position will remain open until filled but only applications received by November 2, 2006. Applications may be submitted at the following link: https://www.academicsearch.org/JuniataProvostApply . Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/12/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1859": {
      "title": "Network Administrator",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Network Administrator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Network Administrator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Network Administrator position is primarily on campus and requires regular in-person attendance. Occasional hybrid work opportunities may be available based on operational needs and approval. This position is not budgeted for visa sponsorship. The role includes administrative and privileged access to critical College technology systems and requires a high degree of responsibility, discretion, confidentiality, and integrity. Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Juniata’s full-time benefits package prioritizes the well-being and work-life balance of employees: medical; vision; dental; retirement (403b); paid vacation, sick leave, holiday time; tuition benefit (employee, spouse, and dependents); wellness programming; additional insurance programs. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Network Administrator Posting Number 20110685 Pay Rate Starting at $70K, final offer commensurate with experience Position Type Administration Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College, a nationally ranked liberal arts institution located in Huntingdon, Pennsylvania, seeks a Network Administrator to join our collaborative and innovative Administrative Information Systems ( AIS ) team. The Network Administrator is responsible for the operation, reliability, security, and continued development of Juniata College’s campus network and related communications infrastructure. This position serves as the primary technical resource for wired and wireless networking and is responsible for administering, monitoring, troubleshooting, and improving the College’s network environment. The position combines day-to-day network operations with opportunities to design and implement infrastructure improvements, contribute to network security and resiliency, and provide technical leadership for network-related projects. As part of a small, collaborative ITS organization, the Network Administrator will also work across infrastructure, systems, security, and support areas as needed. Key Responsibilities Administer, monitor, maintain, and troubleshoot campus wired and wireless networks, including switching, routing, wireless, Internet connectivity, and associated network services. Administer and optimize the College’s centralized network management environment, including Aruba Central. Monitor network availability, capacity, performance, and security and proactively address potential issues. Plan, design, and implement network improvements and lifecycle replacements that enhance reliability, capacity, redundancy, security, and operational efficiency. Administer and support network security technologies and controls, including firewalls, VPN /remote access, network segmentation, wireless security, network authentication, NAC , and 802.1X. Plan and support physical network infrastructure, including copper and fiber-optic cabling, telecommunications spaces, network equipment, and associated backup power. Provide network design and implementation expertise for new construction, renovations, and other campus projects. Participate in disaster recovery and business continuity planning, implementation, documentation, and testing for network and communication services. Lead or provide technical leadership for network-related projects and coordinate work with vendors, telecommunications providers, and contractors. Evaluate emerging networking technologies and recommend solutions appropriate to the College’s technical, operational, and financial requirements. Create and maintain network diagrams, configurations, standards, procedures, and other technical documentation. Collaborate with Information Security and other ITS staff to identify risks, implement appropriate safeguards, troubleshoot complex issues, and continuously improve College technology services. Maintain current knowledge of networking, infrastructure, and security technologies and assist with related ITS initiatives as needed. Perform related duties as assigned. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status… EOE Position Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree in information technology, computer science, networking, or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of education, training, certifications, and relevant professional experience. • Professional experience administering and supporting enterprise wired and wireless networks. • Strong knowledge of TCP /IP, routing, switching, VLANs, enterprise wireless networking, and network troubleshooting. • Working knowledge of network security concepts and technologies, including firewalls, VPNs, segmentation, authentication, and access controls. • Knowledge of structured copper cabling, fiber-optic networking, and wireless infrastructure. • Experience with network monitoring and diagnostic tools and demonstrated ability to independently troubleshoot complex technical issues. • Ability to evaluate technical requirements and implement solutions in a production environment. • Strong communication and documentation skills, including the ability to communicate with both technical and non-technical audiences. • Ability to work independently and collaboratively, manage multiple priorities, and learn new technologies. • Strong judgment, responsibility, and integrity appropriate to a position with privileged access to critical institutional infrastructure. • Ability to respond to critical network or system outages outside normal working hours when required. Supervision Required/Given This position reports to the Assistant Chief Information Officer and works under general guidelines and direction. The Network Administrator is expected to exercise independent technical judgment while collaborating closely with other ITS staff. The position may provide technical direction to student employees, contractors, vendors, or other staff involved in network-related projects but does not necessarily have formal supervisory responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications Experience in one or more of the following areas is preferred: Aruba enterprise networking products and Aruba Central. Enterprise wireless design and optimization. NAC , 802.1X, and certificate-based network authentication. Next-generation firewalls, VPNs, and network segmentation. Network monitoring, logging, packet analysis, or configuration management. High-availability networking and redundant Internet connectivity. Campus fiber infrastructure and structured cabling. Disaster recovery or secondary-site networking. Network automation, scripting, or APIs. Networking within higher education, a multi-building campus, or a similarly complex enterprise environment. Relevant networking or network security certifications. Physical Demands After-hours and on-call support is required for emergencies, critical outages, and planned maintenance. Work may take place in offices, classrooms, residence halls, telecommunications rooms, equipment rooms, and other campus infrastructure spaces. Duties may require using ladders, accessing cabling above ceilings or below floors, installing and troubleshooting network equipment, and moving between campus buildings. Must be able to lift, carry, push, or position equipment weighing up to 40 pounds. Special Instructions to Applicants The Network Administrator position is primarily on campus and requires regular in-person attendance. Occasional hybrid work opportunities may be available based on operational needs and approval. This position is not budgeted for visa sponsorship. The role includes administrative and privileged access to critical College technology systems and requires a high degree of responsibility, discretion, confidentiality, and integrity. Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Juniata’s full-time benefits package prioritizes the well-being and work-life balance of employees: medical; vision; dental; retirement (403b); paid vacation, sick leave, holiday time; tuition benefit (employee, spouse, and dependents); wellness programming; additional insurance programs. Posting Detail Information Open Date 10/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
